<rss version="0.92"><channel><item>
            <title>[LU-21178] client lu_object hash grows without bound and wedges rhashtable resizing</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-21178</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;The client hashes every stripe object of every cached inode in a single&lt;br/&gt;
rhashtable, and that table has no upper bound.  When it grows past 100.7M&lt;br/&gt;
objects the next resize asks for 2 GiB, which the kernel refuses; the resize&lt;br/&gt;
worker retries the allocation forever and the node spends its CPUs there.&lt;br/&gt;
Independently, the code path that reacts to a full table cannot make progress&lt;br/&gt;
and would spin forever, so any attempt to cap the table without also fixing&lt;br/&gt;
that path turns a warning storm into a hang.&lt;/p&gt;
</description>
                <environment />
