                            <comment id="505622" author="bobijam" created="Tue, 10 Nov 2026 15:59:05 +0000">&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://review.whamcloud.com/c/fs/lustre-release/+/70674" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;https://review.whamcloud.com/c/fs/lustre-release/+/70674&lt;/a&gt; &lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-21178" title="client lu_object hash grows without bound and wedges rhashtable resizing" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-21178"&gt;LU-21178&lt;/a&gt; obdclass: do not retry a full object hash forever&lt;br/&gt;
&lt;a href="https://review.whamcloud.com/c/fs/lustre-release/+/70675" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;https://review.whamcloud.com/c/fs/lustre-release/+/70675&lt;/a&gt; &lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-21178" title="client lu_object hash grows without bound and wedges rhashtable resizing" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-21178"&gt;LU-21178&lt;/a&gt; lov: use a separate lu_site per lovsub device&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;These do not cover:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;A per-site object cap, sized well below the rhashtable threshold, with a&lt;br/&gt;
  drop-inode policy behind it (EX-16399).  Without such a cap the fix above&lt;br/&gt;
  only makes the wall much less likely: one hot OST, a few-OST filesystem or&lt;br/&gt;
  wide striping can still fill one table.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Making &lt;tt&gt;lu_cache_nr&lt;/tt&gt; apply per site, or replacing it with a real per-site&lt;br/&gt;
  limit; with N sites the current per-site check against a node-global value&lt;br/&gt;
  allows N times as many objects.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
</comment>
                            <comment id="505647" author="bobijam" created="Wed, 11 Nov 2026 08:26:01 +0000">&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://review.whamcloud.com/c/fs/lustre-release/+/70708" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;https://review.whamcloud.com/c/fs/lustre-release/+/70708&lt;/a&gt; &lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-21178" title="client lu_object hash grows without bound and wedges rhashtable resizing" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-21178"&gt;LU-21178&lt;/a&gt; obdclass: skip idle sites when walking the cache&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
